 R←Test_24(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;wsid;Folder;local;exe
⍝ `CheckErrorFolder` names the default folder after the WS, the EXE or "ERROR_WS", and leaves ⎕WSID alone
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

⍝ Preconditions...
 wsid←⎕WSID
 Folder←{
     parms←##.HandleError.CreateParms
     parms.checkErrorFolder←0
     _←##.HandleError.CheckErrorFolder parms
     parms.errorFolder
 }

 :If 'Win'≡APLTreeUtils2.GetOperatingSystem ⍬
     local←2 ⎕NQ'.' 'GetEnvironment' 'LOCALAPPDATA'
     exe←2⊃⎕NPARTS{'"'∊⍵:1↓⍵/⍨1=+\'"'=⍵ ⋄ ⍵↑⍨¯1+⍵⍳' '}2 ⎕NQ'#' 'GetCommandLine'

     ⎕WSID←'C:\apps\MyApp.dws'
     →T.GoToTidyUp(FilesAndDirs.NormalizePath local,'/MyApp/Errors')≢Folder 0
     →T.GoToTidyUp ⎕WSID≢'C:\apps\MyApp.dws'

     ⎕WSID←'CLEAR WS'
     →T.GoToTidyUp(FilesAndDirs.NormalizePath local,'/ERROR_WS/Errors')≢Folder 0
     →T.GoToTidyUp ⎕WSID≢'CLEAR WS'

     ⎕WSID←''
     →T.GoToTidyUp(FilesAndDirs.NormalizePath local,'/',exe,'/Errors')≢Folder 0
     →T.GoToTidyUp ⎕WSID≢''
 :Else
     ⎕WSID←'/apps/MyApp.dws'
     →T.GoToTidyUp(FilesAndDirs.PWD,'/Errors')≢Folder 0
     ⎕WSID←''
     →T.GoToTidyUp(FilesAndDirs.PWD,'/Errors')≢Folder 0
     →T.GoToTidyUp ⎕WSID≢''
 :EndIf

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 ⎕WSID←wsid
